<title>JAPAN: Fujisawa Pharm to expand Prograf sales in Europe.</title>
<headline>Fujisawa Pharm to expand Prograf sales in Europe.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fujisawa Pharmaceutical Co Ltd said on Friday that it expects to start selling its immuno-depressant drug Prograf in Italy, the Netherlands and Finland before the end of this year.</p>
<p>The major Japanese drug maker already markets Prograf, used in organ transplants, in 10 European countries including Britain and Germany.</p>
<p>The company also hopes to begin selling the drug in Belgium next year, a Fujisawa spokesman said.</p>
<p>The spokesman said that sales of Prograf in the U.S. market are expected to total around $90 million in 1997.</p>
<p>The drug was first launched in Japan in June 1993.</p>
</text>
